.TH MFCJ5720DW-MONITOR 1 "November 2026" "mfcj5720dw-cups 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mfcj5720dw-monitor \- monitor a Brother MFC-J5720DW network printer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mfcj5720dw-monitor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display physical printer status, diagnostic messages, four ink levels and
recent jobs belonging to the current user in a local CUPS queue.
Poll the printer and CUPS every five seconds without blocking the window.
The monitor sends no print data, maintenance commands or SNMP writes.
.PP
Desktop notifications report new faults, recovery, a paused queue and
observed job delivery, cancellation or failure.
Two consecutive failed polls trigger a connectivity notification.
An unavailable measurement is displayed as unavailable, never as zero ink.
The initial job list does not generate notifications for old completed jobs.
.PP
The window can remain running when closed. Use Quit monitor to stop it;
launch it again to reopen the window. Login startup is an explicit preference.
Use Apply to save preferences and the selected printer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-queue " " \fIQUEUE\fR
Follow this local CUPS queue. Otherwise use the saved selection or the first
MFC-J5720DW queue. CUPS is contacted through its local Unix socket.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " " \fIHOST\fR
Query this bare host name, IPv4 or IPv6 address.
Do not include a URI scheme, brackets or a port.
Without an override, derive the address from a socket, LPD, IPP or IPPS queue.
For a DNS-SD service URI, USB queue or print-server URI, enter the physical
printer's address explicitly. The printer must be reachable over the network.
.TP
.BR \-\-community " " \fICOMMUNITY\fR
SNMP read community (default: public). SNMPv2c queries use UDP port 161.
The community is saved in a private user settings file when Apply is used.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start monitoring without showing the window.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Print a single textual status report and exit. No graphical session is needed.
Exit status is 0 on an SNMP reply, 1 when unavailable, or 2 for invalid options.
A successful query can still report a printer fault or unsupported diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.SH LIMITATIONS
CUPS completion means that the backend finished sending the job. It is not
proof that the printer has finished producing all sheets. A job disappearing
from CUPS history is not treated as successful completion.
.PP
The printer's display text and diagnostic state also reflect maintenance.
The monitor does not infer completion of a particular cleaning operation from
an idle state and does not offer an alignment wizard.
Unknown Brother status codes remain visible with the printer's own message.
Alerts and job history are bounded to 16 and 20 entries per query respectively.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mfcj5720dw-monitor/settings.ini
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/io.github.vivier.mfcj5720dw.monitor.desktop
.PP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME defaults to ~/.config.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mfcj5720dw-monitor --queue Brother-MFC-J5720DW
mfcj5720dw-monitor --host 192.168.100.2 --once
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lpstat (1),
.BR commandtomfcj5720dw (1)
